{"step_index":2078,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T07:52:18Z","input_tokens":6439,"cache_read_tokens":78445,"output_tokens":2564,"thinking":"Considering how to augment the sorting options within the problem explorer and dedicated topic page views. The focus is to integrate learning order sorting, both ascending and descending, alongside title-based sorting. This aims to provide users with more control over the presentation of content, aligning with different learning preferences or search strategies.\n\n\nImplementing sort options for title (Z-A), difficulty (easy to hard, hard to easy), and LeetCode number (ascending, descending) will enhance content organization.  The existing HTML structure indicates how to visually represent the sorting dropdown and status filter pills, and they can serve as a reference.\n\n\nPagination controls and page size options will be integrated within the table rendering function. The existing HTML structure provides a clear template for implementing these features. This design will allow the display to handle a variable number of problems.\n\n\nPagination control implementation necessitates adding navigation elements for first, previous, next, and last pages, along with page number indicators, adjusting logic to simplify control display when all items are shown.  Size selection change will update the current page and re-render the problem table, triggered by a listener.\n\nRoute handling will be reviewed. Cases include #dsa/problem/:id, #problem/:id, #dsa/topic/:name and #dsa; problem and topic detail display are invoked based on the route match, verifying the problem or topic's availability.\n\n\nA unique route badge and copy route link button will be integrated within the problem modal header for easy sharing. When the copy button is clicked, the current URL, appended with the problem ID, will be copied to the clipboard.  A confirmation toast will indicate successful copy.\n\nThe problem import functionality will be enhanced by adding deduplication based on problem ID, LeetCode number, normalized title, and the source URL to avoid importing duplicate entries. This will be implemented during the import process.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\app_build\\dsa_dashboard.js","EndLine":1020,"StartLine":900,"toolAction":"Viewing metrics grid in render()","toolSummary":"View metrics grid"}}]}
